<title>USA: Detroit Ed to restore all service tonight.</title>
<headline>Detroit Ed to restore all service tonight.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Detroit Edison said Tuesday it expects to restore service by late tonight to the less than 5,000 electricity customers still without power.</p>
<p>Severe ice storms last Thursday night in southeastern Michigan resulted in more than 422,000 power outages out of a total of more than two million Detroit Edison customers.</p>
<p>Early Monday the company said about 37,000 customers were still without service.</p>
<p>Detroit Edison is a subsidiary of DTE Energy Co.</p>
<p>((--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
